{"id":"concert-tours","title":"Highest-grossing concert tours","prompt":"Name the 10 highest-grossing concert tours of all time (not adjusted for inflation)","noun":"concert tours","category":"Entertainment","metric":"Gross (US$)","blitz":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: List of highest-grossing concert tours","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_highest-grossing_concert_tours","asOf":"2026-11-02"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"The Eras Tour","aliases":["Taylor Swift","The Eras","Taylor Swift's The Eras Tour","Era Tour"],"value":"$2,077,618,725","n":2077618725,"article":"The Eras Tour","fact":{"text":"After the first US leg, Taylor Swift gave $100,000 bonuses to each of the 50 truck drivers hauling the stage.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Eras_Tour"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Music of the Spheres World Tour","aliases":["Music of the Spheres","Coldplay","MOTSWT","MOTS World Tour","MOTS Tour","MOTS"],"value":"$1,524,423,018","n":1524423018,"article":"Music of the Spheres World Tour","fact":{"text":"Coldplay planted a tree for every ticket sold and cut the tour's emissions by 59% compared with their previous one.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_the_Spheres_World_Tour"}},{"rank":3,"name":"After Hours til Dawn Tour","aliases":["After Hours til Dawn","The Weeknd","After Hours Tour","The After Hours World Tour","After Hours til Dawn Stadium Tour","After Hours till Dawn","After Hours till Dawn Tour","The Weekend"],"value":"$1,070,000,000","n":1070000000,"article":"After Hours til Dawn Tour","fact":{"text":"Its stage was a row of ruined buildings modelled on the Weeknd's hometown, Toronto.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_Hours_til_Dawn_Tour"}},{"rank":4,"name":"Farewell Yellow Brick Road","aliases":["Elton John","Farewell Yellow Brick Road Tour","Farewell Tour"],"value":"$939,100,000","n":939100000,"article":"Farewell Yellow Brick Road","fact":{"text":"Its Dodger Stadium show, streamed on Disney+, won the Emmy that completed Elton John's EGOT.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farewell_Yellow_Brick_Road"}},{"rank":5,"name":"Mathematics Tour","aliases":["Ed Sheeran","Sheeran"],"value":"$875,700,000","n":875700000,"article":"Mathematics Tour","fact":{"text":"Its logo first appeared on Ipswich Town shirts, sponsored by Ed Sheeran, four months before the tour was announced.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%2B%E2%88%92%3D%C3%B7%C3%97_Tour"}},{"rank":6,"name":"Divide Tour","aliases":["Ed Sheeran","Sheeran"],"value":"$776,200,000","n":776200000,"article":"Divide Tour","fact":{"text":"Ed Sheeran sold more than 300,000 tickets for seven shows in Ireland in a single day, a first there.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%B7_Tour"}},{"rank":7,"name":"360° Tour","aliases":["U2 360° Tour","U2360 Tour","U2360","U2360 degrees tour","360 Degree Tour","U2 360 Degree Tour","U2 360 Degrees Tour","360 Degrees Tour","U2 360","U2"],"value":"$736,421,586","n":736421586,"article":"U2 360° Tour","fact":{"text":"U2's 2009 Rose Bowl show was the first concert streamed live on YouTube, watched by nearly 10 million.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U2_360%C2%B0_Tour"}},{"rank":8,"name":"Springsteen and E Street Band 2023–2025 Tour","aliases":["2023–2025 Tour","Springsteen and E Street Band 2023–2025","Bruce Springsteen","Springsteen"],"value":"$729,700,000","n":729700000,"article":"Springsteen and E Street Band 2023–2025 Tour","fact":{"text":"COVID kept Nils Lofgren out of a Houston show, the first he had missed since joining the E Street Band in 1984.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Springsteen_and_E_Street_Band_2023%E2%80%932025_Tour"}},{"rank":9,"name":"M72 World Tour","aliases":["M72 Tour","M72","Metallica"],"value":"$668,400,000","n":668400000,"article":"M72 World Tour","fact":{"text":"At Virginia Tech, Metallica fans jumping to \"Enter Sandman\" registered as a small earthquake.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M72_World_Tour"}},{"rank":10,"name":"Love On Tour"